  "hits": [
    {
      "path": "docs/development_report.md",
      "line": 9,
      "kinds": [
        "protocol_capture_audit"
      ],
      "text": "The protocol layer validates bounded frames, checks XOR checksums and parses exact decimal, coordinate, date and time values. Seven sentence codecs convert validated frames into typed records and canonical output. Unknown validated records remain raw evidence.",
      "excerpt_start_column": 1,
      "match_column": 5
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-07-nmea-toolkit.md",
      "line": 7,
      "kinds": [
        "protocol_capture_audit"
      ],
      "text": "**Architecture:** A portable protocol core validates bounded caller-provided input and produces typed records. Separate deterministic state machines assemble multipart GSV evidence and fuse same-time navigation records; track modules then derive geographic metrics and diagnostics without hidden I/O. Batch, integrity and report modules expose reproducible evidence for examples and acceptance.",
      "excerpt_start_column": 1,
      "match_column": 30
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-07-nmea-toolkit-design.md",
      "line": 21,
      "kinds": [
        "protocol_capture_audit"
      ],
      "text": "emitting stable reports. The library targets offline processing, protocol tests,",
      "excerpt_start_column": 1,
      "match_column": 46
    }
